  "provenance_note": "A row listed under self-encoded alone rests on a weaker claim than one under commercial, in two ways. It shows our reader agrees with an independent one on well-formed files at that clock, not that it handles files in the wild. And it is an easier test: the stimulus was decoded through our own filter before being re-encoded, so it carries only content that filter passes. Measured agreement is accordingly better on self-encoded cases than on commercial ones, which is a property of the stimulus rather than evidence of a better-behaved reader.",
